E AX3032 596-macro-capture-in-module.ax:32:6-12 macro-capture "the macro's own `dup` is shadowed at this invocation" !"a template's free identifier means what it meant where the macro was WRITTEN (macro-system.md MAC-HYG-6), which qualification enforces by rewriting it to the module that declares it. This one is declared by NO single module - the macro's own does not declare it, and it is not the unique import either - so there was nothing to rewrite it to and the binding here would capture it" ?"rename the binding at the call site, or make `dup` unambiguous where the macro is written - declare it in the macro's own module, or import it from exactly one module rather than from several" &AmbMac.ax:11:13-19:"useDup"
